            "heading_text": "Robert Chang",
            "heading_size": "h3-regular",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_ANNWc9": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>Robert leads American Truffle Company with a combination of global business expertise, scientific rigor, and technological innovation—bringing together the skills required to transform truffle cultivation from European tradition into American commercial success.<br/></p><p>With engineering training from Stanford University (B.S. and M.S. in Electrical Engineering, qualified for Ph.D. program, Biology minor), Robert applies systems-level thinking to translate Prof. Paul Thomas's groundbreaking mycorrhizal research into practical A-Z methodology for North American conditions. His technical background enables the data-driven infrastructure that ensures optimal conditions across all ATC partner orchards.<br/></p><p>Before truffles, Robert led global marketing teams at Silicon Valley companies including Yahoo and served as CEO of a software startup—gaining expertise in scaling businesses, building partnerships, and translating complex technology into compelling value propositions and products. He now applies this experience to foster strong relationships with growers, Michelin-starred chefs, media and consumers across North America.<br/></p><p>Fluent in five languages (English, German, Spanish, Mandarin, Japanese), Robert leverages deep industry and cultural understanding with extensive networks across truffle-producing regions in the Americas, Europe, Asia, and Oceania, plus direct access to the industry's three major markets: North America, Asia, and Europe. He is a sought-after speaker at premier truffle events and culinary festivals in the U.S. and Europe—representing American truffle industry on both national and global stages.<br/></p><p>Robert also holds an MBA from Stanford Graduate School of Business and is a Bosch Foundation Fellow. Based in the San Francisco Bay Area, he is passionate about cooking, food innovation, eating well and building a sustainable North American truffle industry through science and partnership. He can often be found eating his way across five continents.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
